==English==

===Etymology===
[[group]] + Itialian diminutive suffix [[-etto]]

===Noun===
'''groupetto''', also used in the definite, as '''the groupetto'''.

# (cycling) A group of riders in a bike race that has been left behind by the main [[peloton]].

# (music) A symbol - looks like the english letter "s" rotated and lie backwards on its belly - used in music notes for musical ornament. This symbol stands for 4 consecutive notes based on the note precedes it, which we'll reffer to here as ''the basic note''. The first note in the group is higher than ''the basic note'', the second is ''the basic note'' itself, the third is lower than ''the basic note'', and the forth is again ''the basic note''. Where the difference between each consecutive notes pair is either a half tone or one whole tone - depending on the musical context.

===Quotations===
'''2005:''' I used to be a master of the groupetto, but it has been many years since I’ve been forced to ride in a bona fide, terminally dropped group. It’s strange to be back. Riding in the groupetto requires a different mentality and skill set. &mdash; Bradley McGee in [http://www.tourdefrancenews.com/tourdefrance/experts/columns/0,5976,s1-12599-527-expert,00.html Riding in the Groupetto]

